# NOTE ON SYNTAX: git does NOT support trailing inline comments. `out/   # checkpoints` is a
# pattern whose literal text includes the spaces and the `#`, so it matches nothing. Four rules
# here were written that way and silently ignored ~1.1 TB of nothing; `git add -A` would have
# staged data/ + teacher_states/ + out/ in full. Comments go on their OWN line. Verify any change
# with: git check-ignore -v <path>

# ---- environments ----
.venv/
vllm/.venv/

# ---- large artefacts: regenerable or huge ----
# trained checkpoints (published on HF), 128G
out/
# preprocessed flow caches, 374G
data/
# collected teacher hidden states, 631G
teacher_states/
# benchmark prompt sets: third-party eval data, kept out of the repo
bench_data/

# ---- logs: keep the pipeline .sh drivers, drop everything else ----
# An allow-list, because the deny-list version kept losing: `logs/*.log` is non-recursive and
# missed logs/async/ and logs/tfa/, and neither covered the 46 empty *_DONE.flag sentinels.
# The ONLY thing in logs/ that belongs in git is the top-level run drivers.
logs/*
!logs/*.sh
scripts/viz/*.log
vllm/*.log
*.out

# ---- rendered media ----
# manim/animation output
media/
scripts/viz/media/
*.mp4
*.zip

# ---- scratch / session dumps ----
newback/
session_*_events.json
interm.html
ar5iv_*.html
untitled.txt
strip.py
tmp/
.claude/
*.orig

# ---- python ----
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.uv-cache/

# ---- model weights: never in git ----
*.pt
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.arrow

# ---- stale vendored copies of upstream vLLM (Apache-2.0) ----
# The tree fork ships as patches/vllm-0.25.1-chained-flow-tree.patch, generated from the
# installed wheel. These _backup/_preopt trees are snapshots of intermediate states, are
# documented as STALE, and put ~1.8 MB of upstream source in the repo with no NOTICE.
vllm/_vllm_backup/
vllm/_vllm_preopt/
vllm/_vllm_preopt2/
vllm/_cf_backup/
